implementationPlan.description:
docs/MCP_SERVER.md, the `### moe.get_commit_scope` section.
Read the inline description task-a2a55bc6 shipped in packages/moe-daemon/src/tools/getCommitScope.ts first, and match its wording.
(a) In the Returns block, right after assigneeProtected, add `finalizingAttempt: { attemptId: string, workerId: string, generation: number } | null,` with an aligned `//` comment that says:
- it is the task's finalizing attempt exactly as claim_next_task's finalizing hold selects it (util/claimEligibility.ts finalizingAttemptsByTask: phase finalizing, non-blank id/taskId/workerId, safe-integer generation >= 1, the highest generation wins);
- it names the attempt whoever holds it, the caller's own included, and is null when there is none;
- it is additive: an older daemon omits it.
(b) Add a Notes bullet right after **Live-assignee protection**, starting **Finalizing hold.** It says:
- the wrapper's owner guard refuses MOE_COMMIT_REFUSED_ACTIVE_ASSIGNEE ('attempt <id> of <worker> is still finalizing') when finalizingAttempt names another worker, and lands when it names the caller's own attempt or is null;
- only an absent field (older daemon), a malformed value (the generation must be an integer, the ids non-blank strings) or the disk fallback sends the wrapper to read every .moe/attempts/*.json record itself, which is the per-landing scan this field replaces;
- the field names the same record that scan would refuse on, because openClaimAttempt closes whatever attempt is open before it opens one, so a task holds at most one finalizing attempt.
Change nothing else in the file. The pending merge's hunks near lines 522, 542 and 1459 are not in this section.
